+Open `SavedCandidateV12d/RoofChimney_ArtistRepair_v12d.blend` or the byte-identical `ExportV12d_Run01/Source/RoofChimney_ArtistRepair_v12d.blend` for editing. The canonical future import packet is `ExportV12d_Run01`: keep its FBX filenames, explicit separate LODs and the historical double `.png.png` texture suffixes unchanged. No regeneration is required to use the supplied export bytes. Packed images provide the editable source's image closure.
+
+Historical JSON/proofs retain their original absolute author paths and intermediate status strings verbatim. They are provenance, not portable scripts, runtime dependencies or current production claims. The location-dependent author recipes/installed Engine audit prerequisites are outside the100 payloads and are not included as a reproducible-from-scratch toolchain. Do not execute old command paths or overwrite immutable evidence.
+
+The final isolated saved-native QA readback passed12LODs/48090triangles/312UCX,25Texture.Source checks and15graphs; it required namespace and typed-UCX reader fixes. Earlier cache/namespace/import and collision-schema failures remain preserved in author QA. This source delivery contains no QA native packages and grants no gameplay approval. Stored TangentY handedness, actual cooked/world collision and roof visual/game acceptance remain pending. Legacy facade material finish remains unfinished. Source-vs-native shading is not parity.
+
+Original source wall/air/outline, material policy and312hulls are retained. Bounded retopology, explicit triangles and authored upper-bevel UV changes are documented in SOURCE_VERSION_CHANGE_INVENTORY_V12D.json and sealed audits. All source/native/art qualifications remain visible.
+
+Future production import is proposed under `/Game/Dink/Refinements/RoofChimneyV12d`, using a fresh bounded import after separate Root approval and world validation. No filesystem package rename, reimport, cook or public native delivery is authorized here. Source provenance follows existing project/upstream terms; this packet does not relicense original Dink references.
